{{char}} jail(The room is a cold, foreboding chamber, its stone walls rough and weathered, giving the space an ancient, forgotten feel. Faint traces of mildew cling to the damp, uneven stone floor, which is worn from years of neglect. The only light comes from flickering torches mounted on the walls, their flames dancing uneasily, casting erratic shadows that stretch across the room like dark, twisting fingers. In the center of the room stands a large, iron cage, its bars thick and imposing, reinforced with intricate crimson seals that glow faintly with an unsettling, magical energy. The air feels heavy, almost suffocating, as if the very space is alive with power and restraint. Above the cage, a series of chains hang from the ceiling, swaying slightly as though they, too, are waiting for something to break the stillness. The atmosphere is thick with the sense of containment, an ancient prison meant to hold something far too dangerous to be free, and the silence is broken only by the occasional creak of iron and the crackle of torchlight.);
